{"seconds": 188.9, "exit": 0, "final": "After Qxf6, Black can just play Qxf6, trading queens. White gains a knight but loses the queen. Net: White gains 3 but loses 9, so -6 for White. That's not good.\n\nSo Qg6+ is indeed the best move!\n\nLet me finalize:\n\n**Best move:** Qg6+\n\n**Coaching note (74 words):**\nWhen attacking a cramped king, look for forcing checks that control escape squares. Qg6+ checks the king while dominating f7 and h7. Black's in a bind: moving to h8 or f8 allows Nxf7# or Qxf7# in the next move. Even if Black captures with fxg6, you recapture Nxe6 with a dominant position. The key lesson: find checks that accomplish multiple things\u2014restricting the king AND controlling critical squares.\n\n**JSON:**\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qg6+\", \"line\": [\"Qg6+\", \"Kh8\", \"Nxf7#\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r2q2k1/2p2p2/p3rn1Q/1p1p2N1/2nP1b2/2PB4/PP3PPP/R4RK1 w - - 3 20"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r2q2k1/2p2p2/p3rn1Q/1p1p2N1/2nP1b2/2PB4/PP3PPP/R4RK1 w - - 3 20"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r2q2k1/2p2p2/p3rn1Q/1p1p2N1/2nP1b2/2PB4/PP3PPP/R4RK1 w - - 3 20"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2q2k1/2p2p2/p3rn1Q/1p1p2N1/2nP1b2/2PB4/PP3PPP/R4RK1 w - - 3 20", "move": "Qh8+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2q2k1/2p2p2/p3rn1Q/1p1p2N1/2nP1b2/2PB4/PP3PPP/R4RK1 w - - 3 20", "move": "Qf8+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2q2k1/2p2p2/p3rn1Q/1p1p2N1/2nP1b2/2PB4/PP3PPP/R4RK1 w - - 3 20", "move": "Bh7+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2q2k1/2p2p2/p3rn1Q/1p1p2N1/2nP1b2/2PB4/PP3PPP/R4RK1 w - - 3 20", "move": "Nxe6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2q2k1/2p2p2/p3Nn1Q/1p1p4/2nP4/2PB4/PP3PPb/R4RK1 b - - 0 20", "move": "Kxh2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r2q2k1/